our ticket bytes independently read from immutable tickets-main9818329740f31f44075b6dc6a8d2171efd8022c9 each say state:review and pr:1512; the earlier review transition was32b61519. They remain review, not done.\n\nThe actual source gate ran unmodified bash tools/check.sh on staged1e7 before code commits, nativeexit0, all children reaped, no cleanup/timeout/interruption. It ended CHECK PASS —1110 steps, none red (396 intentional self-tests). Every working mode/blob and semantic source/index/flags/refs/config guard was exact. Check log, timing footer, node-fixture scope audit/invocations, native process, before/after snapshots and reaper are archived. Its original scope was final combined stagedT4 only; the later native commit receipt proves C4's tree identity, rather than pretending the earlier HEAD already was C4.\n\nThe official unchanged1904 mobile400MiB gate passed on this same staged1e7 source at398.905338287 MiB, nativeexit0 in240.654287483 seconds, all children reaped/no cleanup and source/published/index/refs/config guards exact. Its honest publication HEAD stamp was5cb66944fe. After C4 native republish, the saved C4-VERSUS-MEASURED-TREE-PUBLICATION-DELTA proof checks3405 critical renderer/geometry/terrain/sidecar/picture members exact and the same source tree. Changed publication paths are enumerated: build/entry stamps, pack/prebuilt stamp metadata and tickets. This supports the stated exact-consumer reuse of the real reading; it is not a fresh C4 phone run or whole-publication byte equality. The actual C4 publisher log/reaper and approved V9 root plan are saved.\n\nThe earlier V8 BOTH desktop attempt failed its240-second ready wait before settle or functional capture; mobile did not start. It exited1/reaped all five children with no cleanup, and the wrapper never reached the final global source/published/index/ref guard. Its image, logs, reapers and closed failure record are retained. The subsequent isolated four-core V9 run is not qualified: root has now