combined sources and requalify the actual resulting candidate/current CI tree before merge.\n\nNo source payload duplication is needed: checkpoint757's exact117-row source map restores this very1e7 tree from canonical5cb plus11 saved deltas,99 references755 and7 references756. Its archive EARLY-FOUR-FINAL5CB-1E7-REPAIR-CANDIDATE-WIP-757-20261031 has gzip SHA2569cc3d3b4eaf29373b998c8e84c0aeb44fbb7cd6943ee86025a407cb029cd5858 and availability0bdb3f2a1b24a68e06706c80a3d9b4177c5a439f. Those earlier archives preserve models, true native terrain, images, sources and all failed attempts; all prior evidence leaves remain unchanged.\n\nNext: close and preserve V9 failure/guards, resolve actual public bridge framing and obtain desktop/mobile functional acceptance. Inspect remote smoke conclusions; merge latest canonical dev normally into the feature branch after source-reader closure, preserve foreign work, rederive required generated inputs and qualify the resulting tree. Update PR1512 with actual evidence, satisfy required checks and perform a normal expected-head dev merge when ready; only then settle four tickets/release the owned lap. Historical PR1456 and1486 merges remain complete; the original17 tickets are not all done. This evidence-only checkpoint uses normal fast-forward force:false, lossless RAM gzip with at most4MiB raw parts and immutable all-member readback. It performs no product repository reads/writes, PR/ticket writes, unique asset deletions, force push, admin override or app main merge.\n",
